      "type": "text",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "• If a node crashes before Memtable flush, acknowledged\n  writes can be restored by replaying the CommitLog.\n• This is why CommitLog is critical for durability.\n• On startup, unflushed mutations are re-applied to RAM structures.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 16,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "• If a node crashes before Memtable flush, acknowledged\n  writes can be restored by replaying the CommitLog.\n• This is why CommitLog is critical for durability.\n• On startup, unflushed mutations are re-applied to RAM structures.",
      "lineHeight": 1.35,
      "index": "b1Q"
    },
